{
  "$comment": "Complete planning example for a 15 s vertical Reel; source UI, brand assets, and audio remain proposed. This is not a rendered film. Conventions: frames are the canonical unit (seconds derived; convert with round-half-up, i.e. floor(s*fps + 0.5)). Scene intervals are half-open [start, end), so the last shown frame is end-1. Keyframes are absolute frames inside their scene's [start, end), or inside a layer's [from, until). holdUntil and until are exclusive. Transition overlaps belong to the tail of the outgoing scene; anything that must animate IN during an overlap lives in a layer. Camera poses: x/y are output-pixel translations applied after zoom around 'origin'; 'cut': true jumps to the pose instead of interpolating. Action types: click | tap | hover | type | scroll | drag | system; 'completeAt' is the frame the resulting state is fully settled. Add fields when a project needs them (e.g. measured 'box' geometry); don't rename these. Audio cue 'sync' names what its frame locks to (press | arrival | peak | completeAt | beat | loose); see references/sound-design.md. stagger.from names the origin of a spread: a selector (the action's target), or 'start' | 'end' | 'center'. Replace every 'proposed:' source or selector with a verified one before building. Scene camera poses apply to the stage and scene-space overlays; output-space elements remain fixed. Each subsequent scene starts from the preceding camera pose. Transition owner names a layer ID. Layer zIndex is relative to the output canvas; scene copy defaults to 10. Elements live for their scene interval; interpolate each property between its specified keys and clamp outside them. Later reveals must explicitly start hidden. With no camera pose, use the identity camera.",
